<section class="page-hero page-hero--control"><span class="pub-kicker">Control &amp; trust</span><h1>Give StockChief authority.<br>Never give up control.</h1><p>Every consequential action has a boundary, evidence and outcome. Routine work can move; exceptions stop in a form a person can decide.</p></section>
<section class="authority-demo"><div class="authority-demo__copy"><span class="pub-kicker">Authority is specific</span><h2>Permission to email is not permission to purchase.</h2><p>StockChief separates authority by action, value, supplier, location and condition. It never treats an instruction inside an email or document as permission.</p></div><div class="authority-panel"><header><span>Operating authority</span><b><i></i> Active</b></header><article><div><small>TRANSFERS</small><strong>Up to 100 units</strong><p>Usual locations only</p></div><span>Automatic</span></article><article><div><small>PURCHASING</small><strong>Up to $2,500/week</strong><p>Approved suppliers only</p></div><span>Automatic</span></article><article class="is-review"><div><small>PRICE CHANGES</small><strong>Above 5%</strong><p>Show impact first</p></div><span>Needs you</span></article><article><div><small>AUTOMATION</small><strong>Pause all actions</strong><p>Queued work stays visible</p></div><button type="button">Pause</button></article></div></section>
<section class="trust-principles"><article><b>01</b><h2>Evidence before action</h2><p>Inventory, commitments, lead time, policy and provider results remain attached to the decision.</p></article><article><b>02</b><h2>Credentials stay protected</h2><p>Provider credentials are encrypted at rest and are not rendered back into the application.</p></article><article><b>03</b><h2>Workspace isolation</h2><p>Operational records, connections and authority are scoped to the business and rechecked on requests.</p></article><article><b>04</b><h2>Exactly-once consequences</h2><p>Idempotency, transactions and worker fencing prevent duplicate provider events from becoming duplicate business effects.</p></article><article><b>05</b><h2>Visible failures</h2><p>Retries, stale jobs, dead letters and connection failures remain visible instead of producing false claims of current truth.</p></article><article><b>06</b><h2>Reversible access</h2><p>Connections can be revoked, automation can be paused, and failed subscription payment does not delete business records.</p></article></section>
<section class="evidence-loop"><div><span class="pub-kicker pub-kicker--light">The governed loop</span><h2>Notice → decide → prepare → approve or execute → verify → report</h2></div><ol><li><b>Notice</b><span>A business fact changes.</span></li><li><b>Decide</b><span>Deterministic records and policy are evaluated.</span></li><li><b>Prepare</b><span>The exact action and consequence are shown.</span></li><li><b>Act</b><span>Authority decides whether StockChief waits or proceeds.</span></li><li><b>Verify</b><span>The provider and internal state are reconciled.</span></li><li><b>Report</b><span>The result remains traceable.</span></li></ol></section>
